//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Last Man Standing V2, the Game Server reads this file instead of LastManStanding.xml when it exists
//~~ Event phases: registration, preparation (registered players are moved into their rooms), battle, end with rewards, move to town
//~~ The IGC Client shows registration, battle and result windows, the classic client gets chat notices
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### LastManStanding ###
//	Enable: Whether or not, activate the event, 0/1
//	AllowSameIPUser: Whether or not, allow different players from same IP to access same room twice or more at the same time, 0/1
//	AllowSameHWIDUser: Whether or not, allow different players from same computer (HWID) to access same room twice or more at the same time, 0/1
//	DamageReductionLimit: Maximum damage reduction that can be achieved during event battle
//	MinPlayers: Minimum number of players in a room to start its battle, minimum is 2, a room with fewer players is cancelled and the fees are refunded
//	MaxPlayers: Maximum number of players per room, 2-50
//
// ### LastManStanding::Reward ###
//	RewardOnTimeOver: Whether or not, reward players when battle time is over and two or more players are left in the room, 0/1
//	BestScoreWinner: Whether or not, the player with the most kills among players left in the room wins when battle time is over, equal kills are decided by fewer deaths, 0/1
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ If BestScoreWinner is enabled then RewardOnTimeOver is getting set to 1 automatically
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//	MaxUsersToReward: Number of best ranked players to reward, eliminated players included, -1 for no limit
//	WinnerNeedsKill: Whether or not, the last player left or the best score player wins only with at least one kill, 0/1
//	RewardLeavers: Whether or not, players who left the battle (log out, map change) get the reward of a loser at the end, 0/1
//
// ### LastManStanding::Event ###
//	Duration: Duration of the battle, minutes
//	PrepareSeconds: Time between the end of registration and the start of the battle, players are moved into their rooms during it, 10-600 seconds
//	TownSpawn: Time after which players will be moved back to town after event ends, seconds
//	MapNumber: Map number the event runs on
//	TownGate: Gate used to move players to town, see Warps\Gate.xml
//	TeleportsPerTick: Number of players moved into the rooms at once, every 100 milliseconds, 1-50
//
// ### LastManStanding::Registration ###
//	Time: Duration of registration period, minutes
//	MapNumber: Map number to spawn the registration NPC on
//	NPCIndex: Index of Event Registration NPC
//	PosX: The X coordinate of the Registration NPC
//	PosY: The Y coordinate of the Registration NPC
//	Dir: Direction the Registration NPC looks at after spawn
//		~ 0: Central
//		~ 1: South-West
//		~ 2: South
//		~ 3: South-East
//		~ 4: East
//		~ 5: North-East
//		~ 6: North
//		~ 7: North-West
//		~ 8: West
//		~ -1: Random
//
//	ReqMoney: Amount of Money (Zen) to register for the event
//	ReqSpecialItem: Defines if a special item is required prior to register to the event, 0/1
//	ItemCount: Count of special items required, ignored if ReqSpecialItem is set to 0
//	ItemCat: Category of required item for registration, refer to ItemList.xml, ignored if ReqSpecialItem is set to 0
//	ItemIndex: Index of required item for registration, refer to ItemList.xml, ignored if ReqSpecialItem is set to 0
//	ItemLevel: level of required item, 0-15, ignored if ReqSpecialItem is set to 0
//	AllowCancel: Whether or not, players of the IGC Client can cancel the registration while it is open and get the Zen and items back, 0/1
//	NpcRange: Maximum distance to the registration NPC to register in the IGC Client window, 1-30 tiles
//	WindowSeconds: Time the IGC Client registration window can be used after talking to the NPC, 10-3600 seconds
//
// ### LastManStanding::Schedule::Start ###
//	Hour: Start hour of the event, 0-23
//	Minute: Start minute of the event, 0-59
//	DayOfWeek: Day of week the event starts on
//		~ -1: Every day
//		~ 0: Sunday
//		~ 1: Monday
//		~ 2: Tuesday
//		~ 3: Wednesday
//		~ 4: Thursday
//		~ 5: Friday
//		~ 6: Saturday
//
// ### LastManStanding::Zone ###
//	Shrinking safe zone of every room without its own Zone, the zone is off when the element is not there
//	Enabled: Whether or not, activate the shrinking safe zone, 0/1
//	DamagePercent: Damage taken by a player outside the zone, percent of maximum life, 0-100
//	DamageMin: Minimum damage taken by a player outside the zone
//	TickMs: Time between two damage hits, 250-5000 milliseconds
//	WarningSeconds: Time before a step begins when players are warned, 0-60 seconds
//
// ### LastManStanding::Zone::Step ###
//	The zone starts as the room (Coordinates StartX, StartY, EndX, EndY) and every step makes it smaller, up to 16 steps
//	Start: Time after the start of the battle when the step begins, seconds
//	Duration: Time the zone takes to reach the size of the step, seconds, 0 for at once
//	Shrink: Number of tiles the zone loses on every side
//	X1, Y1, X2, Y2: Exact area of the zone after the step, used in place of Shrink
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ A step that ends after the battle or whose area is not inside the area of the previous step is skipped
//~~ The classic client does not show the zone, its players get chat notices with the area that stays safe
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//
// ### LastManStanding::RoomSettings::Room ###
//	ID: Unique ID of the room in range of 0-19
//	KickDieCount: Number of times being killed to kick from the event
//	DamageReduction: Damage reduction during the event, 1-100, read DRMultiplyByKillPoint description
//	DRMultiplyByKillPoint: Multiply damage reduction value by kill points, 0/1
//		~ 0: Damage reduction formula: AttackDamage = AttackDamage * DamageReduction / 100
//		~ 1: Damage reduction formula: AttackDamage = AttackDamage * (100 - (DamageReduction - (DamageReduction * KillPoint))) / 100
//
// ### LastManStanding::RoomSettings::Room::Coordinates ###
//	StartX: Start X coordinate of specified room
//	StartY: Start Y coordinate of specified room
//	EndX: End X coordinate of specified room
//	EndY: End Y coordinate of specified room
//	RebornStartX: Start X coordinate to move/respawn players upon event start and after death, inside the room
//	RebornStartY: Start Y coordinate to move/respawn players upon event start and after death, inside the room
//	RebornEndX: End X coordinate to move/respawn players upon event start and after death, inside the room
//	RebornEndY: End Y coordinate to move/respawn players upon event start and after death, inside the room
//
// ### LastManStanding::RoomSettings::Room::Requirements ###
//	MinLevel: Minimum level to join to specific room, value must be greater or equal value of PlayerKillSystem.xml::MinLevelForPK
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ If set to 'MinLvlForPK' then MinLevel will be set to value of value of PlayerKillSystem.xml::MinLevelForPK
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//	MaxLevel: Maximum level to join to specific room, if set to MAX the value will be set to sum of max regular and master level for server
//	MinGrandReset: Minimum number of grand resets to qualify for specified room
//	MaxGrandReset: Maximum number of grand resets to qualify for specified room
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//~~ Grand resets must be maintained by your web module. It is just data stored in Character table
//~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
//	MinReset: Minimum number of resets to qualify for specified room
//	MaxReset: Maximum number of resets to qualify for specified room, if 'MAX' is used then it is set to value of ResetSystem.xml::MaxReset
//
// ### LastManStanding::RoomSettings::Room::Zone ###
//	Shrinking safe zone of this room in place of LastManStanding::Zone, same settings, Enabled set to 0 turns the zone off in this room
//
// ### LastManStanding::RewardSettings::Room ###
//	ID: ID of room the setting applies to, unique in range of 0-19
//
// ### LastManStanding::RewardSettings::Room::Reward ###
//	Up to 50 rewards per room, the reward items go to the Gremory Case
//	MinScore: Minimum score (kills) of the range to issue a reward
//	MaxScore: Maximum score of the range to issue a reward, MAX for no limit
//	LooserEventBagID: Reward to issue to not a winner, -1 if not applies
//	WinnerEventBagID: Reward to issue to a winner, -1 if not applies
//	LooserCP: Gens Contribution point to reward to a looser, 0 to disable, only to players online at the end
//	WinnerCP: Gens Contribution point to reward to a winner, 0 to disable, only to players online at the end
//
// ### LastManStanding::V2 ###
//	Enabled: Whether or not, send the event windows to the IGC Client, 0/1
//
// ### LastManStanding::GmTest ###
//	Times of an event started with the /lmsstart command (Commands.ini [EventsV2]), 0 to use the times set above
//	RegMinutes: Duration of registration, minutes
//	PrepareSeconds: Duration of preparation, seconds
//	DurationMinutes: Duration of the battle, minutes
//
// ### LastManStanding::Strings::String ###
//	Id: Unique message ID, 1-3
//	Text: Text of the message, order and number of placeholders (%d) must be maintained
//
// STRICTLY NO COMMENTS INSIDE TAGS
-->

